# Left out: the return at the end. The early return for one house means
# the other path reaches the end without a return (GAP003). An empty
# street is never mentioned, so nothing handles it.
step 1
add root: dp = [0] * len(nums)
expect gaps WARN001

step 2
add root:
    if len(nums) == 1:
        return nums[0]
expect gaps WARN001 GAP003

step 3
add root:
    dp[0] = nums[0]
    dp[1] = max(nums[0], nums[1])
expect gaps GAP003

# Spoken, "the max of A and B plus C" could group either way; both are accepted.
step 4
add root: for i in range(2, len(nums)~range-bounds):
    dp[i] = max(dp[i - 1], dp[i - 2] + nums[i])
expect gaps GAP003
or
add root: for i in range(2, len(nums)~range-bounds):
    dp[i] = max(dp[i - 1], dp[i - 2]) + nums[i]
expect gaps GAP003

step 5
note root complexity: O(n) time and O(n) space
expect gaps GAP003
